  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_123f0138b0aa4b489aae3eeb36b2f13a",
      "statement": "The build pipeline has two modes: `npm run build` (`tsc -b && vite build`) produces a static SPA in `dist/` with no Electron output, and `npm run build:electron` (`cross-env ELECTRON=1 npm run build && electron-builder --publish never`) activates the Electron main/preload build and packages the desktop app. The `vite-plugin-electron` integration is gated on `ELECTRON=1`; without it `vite` builds only the renderer.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://package.json#L12-L13",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c9809d584a7bcf20f254c4f2ee20ba7d43c50bf8c110250185dc167b1982e080:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://vite.config.ts#L6-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:727da32e242bcc671d1d7938a57389bb48dbd87c28b1706e9628128bb93e4351:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5e6ec9022ce3411987f14f02bf0e1419",
      "statement": "The Electron preload script is emitted as CommonJS with a `.cjs` extension because the package is `type: module`; a `.js`/`.mjs` preload would be treated as ESM while Electron loads preload scripts as CommonJS. Vite's rollup output is forced to `format: cjs` with `entryFileNames: '[name].cjs'`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://package.json#L7-L8",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aecb64e7a648d5586332a41c2706e50a2e6a24b40e14040f83c0b72a59c08464:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://vite.config.ts#L29-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1a9f90c988548be4ab1fe8de7e01b1bf3df66b6ad76e1dc9e3e7c62233c6eed1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d512433d8b114757b964025df55ab19f",
      "statement": "`scripts/ci.sh` is the provider-agnostic single source of truth for CI, running from the repo root under `set -euo pipefail` in order: install (`npm ci` or `npm install`, skippable via `SKIP_INSTALL=1`), typecheck (`npm run typecheck`), wiki-link check (`npm run check:wiki`), tests (`npm test`), and the static SPA build (`npm run build`).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/ci.sh#L1-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ef259eac4c65725fad7661ad2a7ac88eb7c288d986db468469a4d337e67f8724:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_51fff641705d42c6874e4ee2297d91eb",
      "statement": "`.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs `scripts/ci.sh` on `ubuntu-latest` (Node 24) on push to `main` and on every pull request, but deliberately does not add a push-on-every-branch trigger to avoid double-building PR branches. A concurrency group keyed on `${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}` with `cancel-in-progress: true` keeps only the newest run per ref.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/ci.yml#L1-L37",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a4c4e1299cd1d1f88395862622b4c38cf3564f4a519e06fc67d32e0981e7e938:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1df55825edbc48c18babb2ccbe614a53",
      "statement": "The integration and e2e tests live in a reusable workflow `integration-tests.yml` (`workflow_call`/`workflow_dispatch`) separate from per-PR CI. The `integration-test` job runs the jsdom-based `test:integration` suite (which mocks the platform seam), while the `e2e-test` job runs a real packaged-Electron Playwright smoke test (`test:e2e`) under `xvfb-run -a` because Electron opens a real native window on Linux.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/integration-tests.yml#L1-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aaaaf971cfc1dc528037a30d3614eb967e9317f44352003bfaffaa811fa25354:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d3589fe97e6f47fe985c0dc217fbcc32",
      "statement": "The default vitest config excludes the slow integration suite (`*.integration.test.*`) so `npm test` is a fast per-PR unit gate; the integration suite runs separately via `test:integration` with its own `vitest.integration.config.ts`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://package.json#L16-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:41ffe512b1ae703b2055a83646f103908ce81dd207e5c15702d85d5d67cc78bf:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://vite.config.ts#L59-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ddd7210cc88ebf2de4663b3379bc06f4a87afbcd6a93378ef0a724e2ff2b92bd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ba0a9097870140418f883cfd76dbf04c",
      "statement": "`release.yml` triggers on a published GitHub Release (and `workflow_dispatch` dry runs), gates its build job on the reusable `integration-tests.yml` via `uses:`, and runs a per-OS matrix (`fail-fast: false`): macOS produces dmg (arm64+x64), Windows nsis, Linux AppImage, each via `scripts/build-electron.sh`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/release.yml#L1-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3efc42171cd4a59575a7aa22692b564652e11fef0ef34056f41de873294d8486:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_37a8d25f164a472da64ae40ad1ddf0aa",
      "statement": "`release.yml` always uploads artifacts to the workflow run (`if-no-files-found: error`) so manual `workflow_dispatch` builds are downloadable, but attaches them to the release via `softprops/action-gh-release` only when `github.event_name == 'release'`. Windows uploads `*.exe`, `*.exe.blockmap`, `latest.yml`, `latest.yml.sig`; Linux uploads `*.AppImage`, `latest-linux.yml`, `latest-linux.yml.sig`; macOS uploads `*.dmg` with no feed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/release.yml#L88-L102",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4c1b4349be402c4ae02efcf674493bf3bd1186fab1391780bdc232cfa65ce6dd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f7e34d7ad3f74fe39206a0cb86707922",
      "statement": "`scripts/build-electron.sh` mirrors `ci.sh`: runs from the repo root, optionally installs deps (`SKIP_INSTALL=1` to skip), runs `npm run build:electron`, and lists `./release/`. electron-builder auto-detects the host OS and emits the matching target (dmg/nsis/AppImage) into `./release/`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/build-electron.sh#L1-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6be26e29425d5a77129ae222902b5d7d7dd5497824f73656f1317db02893d519:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_67e213c6b89f4660b089279c136f63ac",
      "statement": "Because there is no purchased Authenticode/Apple certificate, `scripts/sign-release.cjs` independently signs the electron-updater feed file (`latest.yml`/`latest-linux.yml`) with an Ed25519 private key from the `RELEASE_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY` secret, writing `<path>.sig` (base64). It runs only on Windows/Linux (macOS has no feed).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/release.yml#L77-L86",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1248e02e77df373c02d3cbef709df7198766fd0716851ee9c4d6af8f1542873c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/sign-release.cjs#L1-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c1c6a1c1f2d0ae0c2d92a769f26a5ec88ac4a6a9c66f44ae4de5550a918c7989:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f8a55064a1f64133ad669b9da05570a5",
      "statement": "The matching release-signing public key is baked into the app at build time (`RELEASE_PUBLIC_KEY_B64` in `src/model/updateSignature.ts`) and never fetched from the release channel, so a compromised release cannot republish a matching fake key. `verifyReleaseSignature` returns false for any malformed key, malformed signature, or genuine mismatch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/model/updateSignature.ts#L28-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0bd526b4a23902a4c7624dab08f8fdc6e7774b42d09e69843fcf2a6305c72535:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0564e5627e2a4c0d93b03b3224188ec4",
      "statement": "At runtime `electron/main.ts`'s `verifyUpdateFeed` fetches the feed file and its `.sig` directly from the release download URL and only proceeds to `autoUpdater.downloadUpdate()` after `verifyReleaseSignature` passes, chaining trust: the project's signature covers the feed file and electron-updater's sha512 check then covers the installer against the now-trusted feed. `autoDownload` and `autoInstallOnAppQuit` are both false, so downloads require an explicit `update:download` and installs require `update:install`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://electron/main.ts#L1235-L1237",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4848955b0c7aa7df90b7e0c2b177d7ed72847731822a22a357b7c1ed4f9e0337:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://electron/main.ts#L1275-L1316",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eb92a9ba1d90ac89e67ab882dbb52f3b019e5d7a3ae18baafe5a8f2792815030:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b359dc5baf3e40d2a9e2810f103bdca4",
      "statement": "Self-update is Windows/Linux only. macOS is excluded because electron-updater's Squirrel.Mac path needs a real Apple Developer ID signature and notarization to pass Gatekeeper, which the project does not have; mac keeps a check-only update banner instead.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://electron/main.ts#L1223-L1241",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7b3e5c10927406bcb95542143add96a46615e7638786fbb3fc24e50e226dc261:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://electron/main.ts#L1294-L1295",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c164b4dfa6d136fe2259bbc2a66a7a40cf755d7ffef04fc08938cb6a807ee04b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e38edea154124cb8b529647fdaf7765e",
      "statement": "The installers themselves are unsigned by Apple/Microsoft. On macOS the `afterPack` hook (`scripts/afterPack.cjs`) applies a free ad-hoc signature (`codesign --force --deep --sign -`) when no `CSC_LINK`/`CSC_NAME` certificate is configured, downgrading the quarantine 'damaged' dead-end to an 'unidentified developer' prompt the user can bypass; if a real certificate is configured the hook returns early so it does not clobber a proper signature.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/afterPack.cjs#L1-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:93c15e81ef4cc7bd3cfc2dd5c119b56939b6a41b07363891aaa7e1022117b20b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_134bd341ad66478d8a9236e022b79123",
      "statement": "The electron-builder `build` config in `package.json` sets appId `io.github.gram21.sailor`, productName `SaiLoR`, asar true, compression maximum, electronLanguages `en-US`, a files list (dist, dist-electron, build/icon.png, excluding maps and node_modules), output dir `release`, the `afterPack` hook, a GitHub publish provider (owner Gram21/repo SaiLoR), and platform targets: macOS dmg arm64+x64, Windows nsis, Linux AppImage, each with a `${productName}-${version}-<os>-${arch}.${ext}` artifactName.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://package.json#L51-L117",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:51ddb3e2490c8c10710fce6e3df1738fd06a36971a2e5d57cbf83fa57123c626:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9605ca1903244305b374bd3d55fd09d5",
      "statement": "`package.json` declares `allowScripts: { \"esbuild@0.25.12\": true }`, permitting only esbuild's install script to run while blocking all other post-install scripts.",
      "evidence": [
