          "resource": "repo://package.json#L118-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:721b13f80ec524911a40161f1b2ca9dc89d98334f7881ec1b3c76b8600b71843:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_59e997597284483d9d67448a3810bd8c",
      "statement": "`Dockerfile.electron` is a build image for the Linux Electron installer using a Debian base (`node:22-bookworm`, not Alpine) because electron-builder needs glibc; it installs `ca-certificates` and `fakeroot`, runs `npm ci`, and defaults to `npm run build:electron`, producing Linux AppImage installers into `/app/release`. Windows/macOS installers must be built on their native OS (Windows can be cross-built by swapping the base for `electronuserland/builder:wine`).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Dockerfile.electron#L1-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4df376afd0f71a53fb1a5677c3ef40320883a5c211db87ee372be23d17b7ba83:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ecf7718793084eef957925a1582d9e27",
      "statement": "`docker-compose.dev.yml` bind-mounts the source at `.:/app` (with a named `/app/node_modules`) so the image only carries toolchain + dependencies; the standard invocation is `docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml run --rm electron`, and the `CMD` can be overridden for other tasks like `npm run build` or `npm test`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docker-compose.dev.yml#L1-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f699737ddd7c6a7789cef5324ef2680be06bbdde9473fd6cdc240872ca88f703:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9c27d5e47c364529828874b8c72e96a0",
      "statement": "`openwiki.yml` is the scheduled weekly (Monday 06:00 UTC) OpenWiki refresh: it stops early unless `main` has relevant (non-`openwiki/**`) commits in the last 7 days, installs `openwiki` plus `mermaid`/`jsdom` for real mermaid-fence validation, runs `openwiki --update --print`, discards the CLI's self-scaffolded `openwiki-update.yml` and `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` snippets, and opens a PR scoped to `openwiki`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki.yml#L1-L99",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5201493cd3da72b9b43ddd1a893da1b3c1bd93a0167112b052f0ae171c7799ee:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4935551a39d0407ea70e00c43c21c122",
      "statement": "`wiki-publish.yml` triggers on push to `main` under `openwiki/**`, `user-guide/**`, `.github/wiki-assets/**`, or the workflow file, and replaces the GitHub wiki with a combined layout: Home landing page, `Development.md` (from `openwiki/Home.md`), flat `openwiki/*.md`, flattened/renamed `user-guide/*.md` (`Guide-*`), and a global `_Sidebar.md`/`_Footer.md` assembled from `.github/wiki-assets/` plus a user-guide fragment. It strips OKF frontmatter, rewrites cross-links for extensionless wiki URLs, and `rsync --delete` mirrors, committing as `github-actions[bot]` with a `[wiki-sync]` marker.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/wiki-publish.yml#L1-L309",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1f22c74ae8393aced6d8a06c5b5575dfa1e5a683b80a4adea4c8c1068de2b580:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_66c08000247f4650aee1ec43741d1cea",
      "statement": "`wiki-import.yml` is the reverse direction, triggering on `gollum` (wiki create/update) and `workflow_dispatch`; it clones the wiki and maps each published piece back to its repo source (`Development.md`→`openwiki/Home.md`, `Guide-*`→`user-guide/<src>.md`, `_Sidebar`/`_Footer` user-guide fragments→`.github/wiki-assets/` lifted out of their `<!-- wiki-sync:NAME:start/end -->` marker pairs), then `rsync --delete` mirrors remaining `*.md` into `openwiki/` and commits to `main` with a `[wiki-sync]` marker.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/wiki-import.yml#L1-L189",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:005b150f9dce6cb48e7e77cd9f74e5932af50823580b4bae732ff30b623bf041:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b09ea28534f1489798a30923839c0643",
      "statement": "Publish and import would otherwise form an infinite loop (publish→gollum→import→main push→publish). Three independent layers prevent it: both share a `concurrency: group: wiki-sync` with `cancel-in-progress: false` so they never run concurrently; `wiki-publish.yml` skips commits whose message contains `[wiki-sync]`; and `wiki-import.yml` skips when `github.event.sender.login == 'github-actions[bot]'`, so each direction only reacts to human-originated changes on the other side.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/wiki-import.yml#L24-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ab79fdb3ae7adddda86fece738cfc584219502441c27d7d38b795885c9317f7c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/wiki-publish.yml#L67-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:98fb6dbf70932bb04d9b39f53c61ab924d7f85f863f12d682ad043418a3fcd3c:"
        }
      ]
    }
